    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap 912 of 1920",
    "lawSection": "Boxing",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER : S3116\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 912 of the laws of 1920,\nrelating to allowing and regulating boxing, sparring and wrestling\nmatches, in relation to the commission quorum required to do business\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo require the presence of the Commissioner of the State Athletic\nCommission who is designated as Chairman in order to constitute a\nquorum so long as there is such a designee or so long as any such\ndesignee is not incapacitated.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThe bill would simply add the requirement that the Chairman of the\nCommission (if a Chairman has been designated or if such designee is\nnot incapacitated) be present to constitute a quorum or to conduct\nbusiness.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nAny two of three commissioners constitutes a quorum.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe person designated as Chairman of the Commission is the only full\ntime commissioner and manages the commission on a day to day basis.\nAs such, no action should be taken without the benefit of his or her\npresence at a commission meeting.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n1993-1994: S. 2663 - Referred to Tourism, Recreation & Sports\nDevelopment\n1995 - 1996:  A.8593/S.4104\n1997 - 1998: A.4659\n1999-2000: A.1617\n2001-2002: A.6078\n2003-2004: A.1384\n2005-2006: A.2337\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
